ng  that should be able to join the cluster  ideally we'd have something like a TPM  that can say here's a cryptographic  assertion that says Who I am and then  write rules about who should be able to  join the cluster and so we've added that  functionality into kubernetes and we're  working on kind of interesting Google  side stuff for that too so yeah no one  else would say yet either but yeah  there's there's more interesting stuff  coming cool so it sounds like a lot of  new cool functionality to make  kubernetes more secure on gke  can you talk more about the bug bounty  program and what we do to discover  vulnerabilities and how we deal with  them yeah so in a few different fronts  Google has its own  bug bounty program right now so you can  if you find a security vulnerability in  gke  or in really any Google product in  within the scope of the bug bounty and  GK is in in scope for the bug bounty  then we will pay you money so please try  out test test the bounds of the GK  security and we're happy to receive  those and we're happy to pay for those  those vulnerabilities  similarly the CNC F is also standing up  its own bug bounty program and that's  currently in process now so we're  working on kind of setting up the  structure for that to be able to handle  those those vulnerabilities coming in  from a program like that and that will  also set kubernetes up in a good place  to also looking at some kind of for  kubernetes in the scene cf is also kind  of looking at some threat modeling and  and that kind of work too so yeah it's  the bug bounty program I think is kind  of a symbol of an organization being  mature enough to know that security bugs  do happen and if we can force x like  taking advantage of that great security  researcher community and paying for them  for their effort it is a lot of effort  to find security vulnerabilities and a  lot of cases then yeah I think it's a  real symbol of maturity and something  that we'd love to see replicated as  