ions for  other customers who are working with  kubernetes or gke and what they can do  to improve their security on their  systems absolutely so one of the ways  that we've been able to do this is by  working really closely with our partners  so whenever we find a vulnerability or  we suspect there may be an opportunity  for a vulnerability then we discuss it  with our partners at Google and we get a  good handle on what the risk of attack  is and what would happen if it were  compromised and if it seems like there's  a high severity there we might be able  to mitigate it on our own platform but  that doesn't help anyone else so we can  release that information or we can  incorporate it into tools we have for  instance an open-source tool called cube  audit that anyone can use and patches  are very welcome and in that way we're  able to improve the security posture  other people can share their knowledge  with us we can share Arnall  with them and in addition to that we  found that one of the biggest things  that prevents people from taking part in  bug bounty programs is low bounties so  if you're not financially compensated  for your work then researchers will move  on to someone else so shop flies very  proud that we offer above-average bug  bounties we offer substantial financial  compensation and in that way when  researchers find problems with our  platform they're encouraged to report it  and they're encouraged to keep coming  back and it really shows that we value  their time and the effort that they put  into it I think that goes a long way to  helping you secure the entire ecosystem  so thank you for that if we could switch  gears a little bit let's talk about cute  con this is not your first coupon no  actually this is the second time that  I've been at cube con I was able to  attend last year in Austin it was my  first time I'd been using kubernetes for  about a month at the time so I was  pretty new but I'm really excited to be  back here today are there any security  related talks that you're excited about  of course yours coming up tomorrow maybe  you want to tell folks about that sure  so there was a specific incident that  happened about six months ago where one  of our security researchers found a  vulnerability in our platform and it  combined a couple of things that may  have seemed like they were low risk on  their own but combined they could have  led to complete control of a cluster and  so we paid our maximum bounty of twenty  five thousand dollars for that and we're  really proud of the work that we did we  received the report and within an hour  and four minutes we were able to  mitigate that vulnerability and I think  that some of the work that we've done  there will be really valuable to others  who are trying to secure their own  platforms so I'm going to be sharing  that alongside my co-presenter Greg and  I'm really excited I think that some of  the details will be valuable I also  really enjoyed seeing my aquezio skis  talk yesterday on security and I think  that was a an incredible talk I thought  one of the most important things that  she covered there was the fact that  there are all of these container escapes  that everyone's really excited about the  really glamorous are sophisticated and  almost no one's using those in the wild  so I was really happy to hear her talk  about  that sounds awesome so if folks are  interested please check out these talks  and thank you so much for your time have  a great rest of your Q con  [Music]

